-linejoin="round"></path><path d="M28 14.5601L37.91 20.2801L28 26.0001L18.09 20.2801L28 14.5601Z" fill="#1C1C22" stroke="#6E6E78" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></g><g><path d="M29.32 38.2L39.23 43.92V32.48L29.32 26.76V38.2Z" fill="#0E0E12" stroke="#6E6E78" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linejoin="round"></path><path d="M49.13 38.2L39.23 43.92V32.48L49.13 26.76V38.2Z" fill="#141419" stroke="#6E6E78" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linejoin="round"></path><path d="M39.23 21.04L49.13 26.76L39.23 32.48L29.32 26.76L39.23 21.04Z" fill="#1C1C22" stroke="#6E6E78" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></g><g><path d="M6.87 38.2L16.77 43.92V32.48L6.87 26.76V38.2Z" fill="#0E0E12" stroke="#6E6E78" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linejoin="round"></path><path d="M26.68 38.2L16.77 43.92V32.48L26.68 26.76V38.2Z" fill="#141419" stroke="#6E6E78" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linejoin="round"></path><path d="M16.77 21.04L26.68 26.76L16.77 32.48L6.87 26.76L16.77 21.04Z" fill="#1C1C22" stroke="#6E6E78" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></g></g><g class="menuIcons-module__jIY1fG__lift"><path d="M18.09 22.7601L28 28.4801V17.0401L18.09 11.3201V22.7601Z" fill="#0E0E12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linejoin="round"></path><path d="M37.91 22.7601L28 28.4801V17.0401L37.91 11.3201V22.7601Z" fill="#141419" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linejoin="round"></path><path d="M28 5.6001L37.91 11.3201L28 17.0401L18.09 11.3201L28 5.6001Z" fill="#1C1C22" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></g></svg><span class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__cardTitle">Careers</span><span class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__cardText">Join us and help build the GPU cloud for everyone.</span></a></div></li><li class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__item"><a class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__trigger" href="/pricing"><span class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__label">Pricing</span></a></li><li class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__item"><a href="https://www.thundercompute.com/docs" class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__trigger" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__label">Docs</span></a></li></ul></nav><div class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__right"><a class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__btn Navbar-module__hPVgWG__btnGhost" href="https://console.thundercompute.com/login" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Log in</a><a class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__btn Navbar-module__hPVgWG__btnSolid" href="https://console.thundercompute.com/signup" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Get started</a><button type="button" class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__burger" data-burger="true" aria-label="Open menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="_R_5bsnpftb_-mnav"><span class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__burgerLine"></span><span class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__burgerLine"></span></button></div></div><nav id="_R_5bsnpftb_-mnav" class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnav" aria-label="Main"><details class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavGroup"><summary class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavRow">Products<svg class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavChevron" viewBox="0 0 16 9" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M.75.75 8 8 15.25.75" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"></path></svg></summary><div class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavSub"><a class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavSubLink" href="/products/instances">Instances</a><a class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavSubLink" href="/products/sandboxes">Sandboxes</a></div></details><details class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavGroup" open=""><summary class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavRow">Resources<svg class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavChevron" viewBox="0 0 16 9" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M.75.75 8 8 15.25.75" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"></path></svg></summary><div class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavSub"><a href="https://www.thundercompute.com/docs" class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavSubLink" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Docs</a><a class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavSubLink" aria-current="page" href="/blog">Blog</a></div></details><details class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavGroup"><summary class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavRow">Company<svg class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavChevron" viewBox="0 0 16 9" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M.75.75 8 8 15.25.75" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"></path></svg></summary><div class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavSub"><a class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavSubLink" href="/mission">About</a><a class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavSubLink" href="/careers">Careers</a></div></details><a class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavRow" href="/pricing">Pricing</a><a href="https://www.thundercompute.com/docs" class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavRow" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Docs</a><div class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__mnavCtas"><a class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__btn Navbar-module__hPVgWG__btnGhost" href="https://console.thundercompute.com/login" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Log in</a><a class="Navbar-module__hPVgWG__btn Navbar-module__hPVgWG__btnSolid" href="https://console.thundercompute.com/signup" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Get started</a></div></nav></header></div><div class="railed-top"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.thundercompute.com/#organization","name":"Thunder Compute","url":"https://www.thundercompute.com","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.thundercompute.com/icon.svg"},"description":"Thunder Compute builds virtualization software that turns underutilized GPUs into additional capacity.","sameAs":["https://x.com/ThunderCompute","https://www.linkedin.com/company/102863366","https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/thunder-9b4c","https://www.producthunt.com/products/thunder-compute","https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/thunder-compute","https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=ThunderCompute.thunder-compute"]},{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.thundercompute.com/#website","url":"https://www.thundercompute.com","name":"Thunder Compute","publisher":{"@id":"https://www.thundercompute.com/#organization"},"potentialAction":{"@type":"SearchAction","target":"https://www.thundercompute.com/search?q={search_term_string}","query-input":"required name=search_term_string"}},{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.thundercompute.com/blog/what-is-ollama-run-ai-models-locally#article","headline":"What is Ollama? Complete Guide to Local AI Models (October 2026)","description":"Ollama is a free, open-source (MIT) tool for running LLMs like Llama, Qwen and DeepSeek locally. See what's free, Ollama Cloud pricing and hardware needs.","url":"https://www.thundercompute.com/blog/what-is-ollama-run-ai-models-locally","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.thundercompute.com/blog/what-is-ollama-run-ai-models-locally","datePublished":"2025-10-17T00:00:00.000Z","dateModified":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","image":"https://www.thundercompute.com/og/blog-v1.png","author":{"@id":"https://www.thundercompute.com/#carl-peterson"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://www.thundercompute.com/#organization"},"isPartOf":{"@id":"https://www.thundercompute.com/blog#blog"},"articleSection":"AI Workflows","keywords":"ollama, local-llm, open-source-ai, ai-inference, gpu-cloud, llm, vram, ollama-models, ollama-cloud, ollama-pricing"},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.thundercompute.com"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Writing","item":"https://www.thundercompute.com/blog"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"What is Ollama? Complete Guide to Local AI Models (October 2026)","item":"https://www.thundercompute.com/blog/what-is-ollama-run-ai-models-locally"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Ollama free?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Ollama is free, open source and unlimited on your own hardware. Ollama Cloud has a free tier, then Pro ($20/mo), Max ($100/mo) and Team ($500/mo) plans with monthly usage credits. Thunder Compute rents a 48GB RTX A6000 for $0.35/hr."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is Ollama Cloud?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Ollama Cloud runs models on Ollama's servers instead of your GPU, through the same CLI and API as local Ollama. Cloud models use a :cloud tag suffix, such as kimi-k2.6:cloud. Run ollama signin once; every request needs an internet connection."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Ollama safe to use?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, when installed from ollama.com or the official GitHub releases. Its API listens only on localhost by default and has no built-in authentication. Never expose port 11434 to the internet without a reverse proxy, VPN or SSH tunnel."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What hardware do I need to run Ollama?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You need a GPU with enough VRAM for your model's precision: about 2GB per 1B parameters at FP16 and 1GB at Q8, plus context. An 8B model at Q8 fits a 12GB GPU. A 32B model at Q8 needs 30-38GB, usually a 48GB cloud GPU."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use Ollama without a GPU?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Ollama supports CPU-only execution, but generation is much slower than on a GPU, especially for models above 7B. Use a dedicated GPU for anything beyond light testing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When should I move from local Ollama to cloud infrastructure?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Move to the cloud when local hardware can't fit the model or precision you need. Cloud GPUs also suit consistent production performance and shared team access to GPU resources."}}]},{"@type":"Blog","@id":"https://www.thundercompute.com/blog#blog","name":"Thunder Compute Writing","url":"https://www.thundercompute.com/blog","inLanguage":"en","publisher":{"@id":"https://www.thundercompute.com/#organization"}},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.thundercompute.com/#carl-peterson","name":"Carl Peterson","jobTitle":"Co-Founder and CEO","worksFor":{"@id":"https://www.thundercompute.com/#organization"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/in/cpeterson42","https://github.com/cpeterson42","https://x.com/carlpeterson"]}]}</script><section class="Doc-module__gMlsRq__section"><div class="Doc-module__gMlsRq__column"><article itemScope="" itemType="https://schema.org/BlogPosting"><header class="Doc-module__gMlsRq__header"><a class="Doc-module__gMlsRq__back" href="/blog">← <!-- -->All writing</a><h1 class="Doc-module__gMlsRq__title Doc-module__gMlsRq__md"><span itemProp="headline">What is Ollama? Complete Guide to Local AI Models (October 2026)</span></h1><p class="Doc-module__gMlsRq__meta">Carl Peterson  ·  October 17, 2025  ·  16 min read</p></header><p hidden="">Ollama is a free, open-source (MIT) tool for running LLMs like Llama, Qwen and DeepSeek locally. See what&#x27;s free, Ollama Cloud pricing and hardware needs.</p><div class="Doc-module__gMlsRq__body Doc-module__gMlsRq__prose"><div class="Post-module__zd2qRG__content" itemProp="articleBody"><p><a href="https://ollama.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ollama</a> is a free, open-source (MIT-licensed) tool for running large language models (LLMs) like Llama, DeepSeek, Qwen and Gemma on your own computer. Local use is free and unlimited. Ollama Cloud adds a free tier that includes a small amount of monthly usage for a set of starter models, plus paid plans from $20/month.</p>
<p>Ollama works through a command-line tool, a desktop app or an OpenAI-compatible API. When a model outgrows your machine, you can run Ollama on a dedicated <a href="https://www.thundercompute.com/pricing" target="_blank">cloud GPU from $0.35/hr</a>.</p>
<p><strong>Takeaways</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Free for local use:</strong> Ollama runs open models on your own hardware at no cost and with no usage limits.</li>
<li><strong>Ollama Cloud is optional:</strong> it offers a free tier with starter credits, then paid plans from $20/month.</li>
<li><strong>Precision drives memory:</strong> <a href="https://medium.com/@laurentkubaski/ollama-model-names-explained-a39460e0fab5" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Most default Ollama tags</a> are 4-bit; Q8 and FP16 need 1.7-3.3x more memory.</li>
<li><strong>Cloud GPUs fill the gap:</strong> Thunder Compute runs Ollama on a 48GB RTX A6000 for $0.35/hr.</li>
</ul>
<h2>What Is Ollama?</h2>
<p><img src="/blog/images/69362a66cc1ed4f4a831b9bf_6903a779a61f2561fa15b9b5_qmz7KN1nk5GAVM2btyHVkjckOM.png" alt="Ollama running a local language model from the command line."></p>
<p>Ollama is an <a href="https://github.com/ollama/ollama" target="_blank" rel="noopener">open-source platform</a> for running and managing LLMs locally or through hosted cloud models. It packages model weights, configuration and a prompt template into a single Modelfile. Pulling and running a model takes one command.</p>
<p>Ollama gives you full control over your models and data, unlike proprietary cloud AI services. The same CLI and API work for local models and for models routed through Ollama&#39;s cloud.</p>
<h3>Who Makes Ollama?</h3>
<p>Ollama Inc. is an independent, <a href="https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/ollama" target="_blank" rel="noopener">venture-backed startup based in Palo Alto, California</a>. Jeffrey Morgan (CEO) and Michael Chiang co-founded the company. The pair <a href="https://betakit.com/kitematic-founders-nab-65-million-usd-to-help-devs-run-ai-models-locally-with-ollama/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">previously built Kitematic, an early graphical interface for Docker</a>.</p>
<p><a href="https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/jmorganca/ollama@v0.1.14" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ollama first launched around Meta&#39;s Llama models</a>, and the name appears to nod to them. Today it runs models from Google, Microsoft, Mistral, DeepSeek, Alibaba (Qwen), Moonshot AI (Kimi) and other labs.</p>
<p>Ollama&#39;s design reflects the founders&#39; Docker background: you pull and run models much like container images.</p>
<h2>Is Ollama Free? Ollama Pricing Explained</h2>
<p>Yes, Ollama is free to download and use. Running models on your own hardware is unlimited and needs no account. The software is <a href="https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/ollama/ollama@v0.8.0-rc0" target="_blank" rel="noopener">released under the MIT license</a>, so commercial use is also free. You pay only for Ollama Cloud, which runs models on Ollama&#39;s servers instead of your GPU.</p>
<p><a href="https://ollama.com/blog/transparent-pricing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ollama Cloud moved to credit-based pricing on August 31, 2026</a>. Each paid plan includes a monthly pool of usage credits, spent at per-token rates that vary by model. Usage continues at the same rates after the included credits run out. The old 5-hour session and weekly limits no longer apply, although existing subscribers can keep their legacy plans.</p>
<p>Ollama Cloud plans as of October 2026:</p>
<div class="Post-module__zd2qRG__tableScroll"><table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Plan</th>
      <th>Price</th>
      <th>Included Usage</th>
      <th style="text-align:center;">Concurrent Requests</th>
      <th>Best For</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Free</td>
      <td>$0</td>
      <td>Starter credits for a set of starter models; unlimited local use</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">1</td>
      <td>Trying cloud models</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Pro</td>
      <td>$20/mo or $200/yr</td>
      <td>$60 of credits per month</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">3</td>
      <td>Daily individual use</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Max</td>
      <td>$100/mo</td>
      <td>$300 of credits per month</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">10</td>
      <td>Running several agents at once</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Team</td>
      <td>$500/mo</td>
      <td>$1K of credits per month, shared across unlimited users</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">10</td>
      <td>Teams with centralized billing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Enterprise</td>
      <td>Custom</td>
      <td>Custom</td>
      <td style="text-align:center;">Custom</td>
      <td>Large organizations</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<p>Unused Ollama Cloud credits do not roll over. Any plan, including Free, can buy extra credits to unlock all models on a pay-as-you-go basis. <a href="https://ollama.com/pricing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ollama&#39;s pricing page</a> lists per-model token rates.</p>
<h3>Ollama Cloud or a Dedicated GPU: Which Costs Less?</h3>
<p>Ollama Cloud is usually cheaper for occasional use, since you pay per token and manage no hardware. A dedicated GPU can be cheaper for long sessions, batch jobs and custom models. The $20 Ollama Pro subscription equals about 57 hours on a Thunder Compute RTX A6000 (48GB VRAM) at $0.35/hr. It also equals about 18 hours on an NVIDIA A100 80GB at $1.09/hr, with no per-token metering.</p>
<p>A dedicated GPU runs any model and precision that fits in VRAM, including fine-tuned GGUF files (llama.cpp&#39;s model format) and full-precision FP16 tags. The trade-off is setup: you size, start and stop a GPU instance, while Ollama Cloud needs only a sign-in.</p>
<h2>Ollama vs Cloud AI: How Do They Compare?</h2>
<p>Ollama wins on privacy, cost control and offline use. Cloud AI services like ChatGPT and Claude win on setup speed and simplicity.</p>
<div class="Post-module__zd2qRG__tableScroll"><table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th></th>
      <th>Ollama (Local)</th>
      <th>Cloud AI (ChatGPT / Claude)</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Data Privacy</strong></td>
      <td>Complete: data never leaves your machine</td>
      <td>Data processed on vendor servers</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Cost</strong></td>
      <td>Free to run; pay only for hardware or GPU time</td>
      <td>Per-token API fees or $20+/month subscriptions</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Internet Required</strong></td>
      <td>Local models: no. Cloud models: yes.</td>
      <td>Yes, always requires a connection</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Model Choice</strong></td>
      <td><a href="https://ollama.com/library" target="_blank" rel="noopener">4,500+ open-weight models</a> (Llama 4, DeepSeek R1, Kimi K2, Mistral and more)</td>
      <td>Limited to the provider's own models</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Setup Time</strong></td>
      <td>About 5 minutes</td>
      <td>Instant (browser-based)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Best For</strong></td>
      <td>Privacy-sensitive work, cost control, offline use, regulated industries</td>
      <td>General use, multimodal tasks, no technical setup</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<p>Choose Ollama when your data can&#39;t leave your infrastructure, API bills are climbing or you need to work offline. Choose cloud AI when you need frontier reasoning or built-in multimodal features without setup.</p>
<h2>How Ollama Works</h2>
<p>Ollama runs as a background service that downloads models, loads them into GPU or system memory and serves them through a local API. It handles model weights, configuration and runtime libraries for you.</p>
<h3>Setting Up Ollama</h3>
<p>Ollama installs and runs a first model in three steps:</p>
<ol>
<li><a href="https://ollama.com/download" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Download the installer</a> from the official Ollama website.</li>
<li>Run the installer and open your terminal.</li>
<li>Run a model: <code>ollama run llama3.2</code></li>
</ol>
<p>After setup, type a prompt and the model responds, much like ChatGPT or Claude.</p>
<p><img src="/blog/images/69362a66cc1ed4f4a831b9cc_6903a779a61f2561fa15b9ac_QTU9J2eMxjhiN9IW2ptGhhF3fzE.png" alt="Terminal chat with an Ollama model running locally."></p>
<h3>CLI, API and Desktop App</h3>
<p>Ollama offers three interfaces to the same local engine and model library: a CLI, a REST API and a desktop app.</p>
<p>The CLI lets you prompt models directly and manage them:</p>
<pre><code class="language-bash">ollama run llama3.1:8b                              # start an interactive chat
ollama run llama3.1:8b &quot;Explain KV cache briefly&quot;   # send a single prompt and exit
ollama pull llama3.1:8b                             # download a model
ollama list                                         # show installed models
ollama ps                                           # show loaded models and the GPU/CPU split
ollama rm llama3.1:8b                               # delete a model
</code></pre>
<p><strong>The REST API serves models to other applications</strong> at <code>http://localhost:11434</code>. Scripts, IDE coding assistants and chat interfaces all talk to Ollama through the REST API, which also accepts OpenAI-style requests.</p>
<p><a href="https://ollama.com/blog/new-app" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>The Ollama desktop app adds a chat window</strong></a> with file and image drag-and-drop for . <a href="https://www.databasemart.com/blog/intro-to-ollama-app-v0100" target="_blank" rel="noopener">On Linux, Ollama is command-line only</a>.</p>
<h3>Ollama&#39;s REST API and OpenAI Compatibility</h3>
<p>Ollama exposes a local REST API at <code>http://localhost:11434</code> that <a href="https://docs.ollama.com/api/openai" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mirrors the OpenAI Chat Completions API</a>. Tools built for OpenAI (LangChain, LlamaIndex, CrewAI, Continue) usually work with Ollama by changing only the base URL. <a href="https://docs.ollama.com/integrations/claude-code" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Claude Code and other Anthropic-compatible tools</a> connect via <code>ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434</code>.</p>
<p>This API compatibility is one of the main reasons developers adopt Ollama over running llama.cpp directly. The same endpoint serves local and cloud-tagged models.</p>
<h2>Ollama Cloud vs Local Models</h2>
<p>Ollama Cloud models run on Ollama&#39;s servers instead of your GPU, through the same CLI and API as local models. Cloud models carry a <code>:cloud</code> suffix (such as <code>kimi-k2.6:cloud</code> or <code>deepseek-v4-pro:cloud</code>). Run <code>ollama signin</code> once, then call them like any local model. Every cloud request needs an internet connection.</p>
<p>Ollama Cloud suits models too large for your hardware and fast inference without GPU management. Local models never send data off your machine. Ollama Cloud requests go to Ollama&#39;s servers, which run primarily in the US and Europe, plus Singapore for a limited set of Qwen models. Ollama says it retains no data and does not log or train on prompts.</p>
